# TypeScript Extension Standards

- Use strict TypeScript and named exports.
- Keep VS Code API imports inside `packages/extension`; shared logic belongs in `packages/core`.
- Feature-detect optional VS Code APIs and provide command/webview fallbacks.
- Respect Workspace Trust: side-effecting features must be disabled when untrusted.
- Store provider credentials and MCP tokens in VS Code `SecretStorage`, never workspace config.
- Do not use `any`; use `unknown` and narrow with explicit checks.
